<problem>
<!-- <title>Cobweb, exponential with two zeros, worksheet</title> -->

<setup>

<math name="zero1">1.</math>
<math name="zero2">3.</math>
<math name="a">2.</math>
<math name="term">exp($zero1 -$a )</math>
<math name="c">($zero2 -$zero1 )/(exp($zero2 -$a )-$term )</math>
<function name="f" variables="x">$c *(exp(x-$a )-$term )+$zero1 </function>
<math name="equilibria" unordered="true">$zero1 ,$zero2 </math>
<math name="infinity_symbol">infinity</math>

</setup>

<p>The function <m>g</m> is plotted below for the dynamical system <m>z_{t+1} = g(z_t)</m>.</p>


<module copy="doenet:83jD1JShkD8umrK9bSc1v8" xmin="-4.5" xmax="4.5" ymin="-1.5" ymax="4.5" function="$f" initialInitialValue="1" x0="0" initialValueDx="0.2" checkInitialCondition="false" showNavigation="false" cobwebbingWeight="0" variable="z" attractThreshold="0.2" grid="true" />


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
Find the equilibria of the dynamical system.  <m>E=</m> 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true">$equilibria </award>
</answer>
  (The equilibria are integers.)
</exercise>

