<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
Use cobwebbing to solve the system with initial condition <m>z_0=-4</m>.  What happens to <m>z_t</m> as <m>t</m> gets large? <m>z_t</m> tends toward 
<answer>
<award>$zero1 </award>
</answer>
.
</exercise>



<solution>


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
The equilibria are <m>E=1,3</m>.
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
As <m>t</m> gets large <m>z_t</m> tends to the equilibrium <m>z=1</m>.
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
As <m>t</m> gets large <m>z_t</m> tends toward infinity.
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
As <m>t</m> gets large <m>z_t</m> tends to the equilibrium <m>z=1</m>.
</exercise>


</solution>


